##### Article 170

Causing Grave or Medium Gravity Harm to Health in Excess of Necessary Defence
1.	Causing medium gravity harm to health of another person in excess of necessary defence —
shall be punished by a fine in the maximum amօunt of ten-fold, or public works for a term of maximum one hundred hours, or restriction of liberty for a term of maximum one year, or short-term imprisonment for a term of maximum one month, or imprisonment for a term of maximum one year.
2.	Causing grave harm to health of another person in excess of necessary defence —
shall be punished by restriction of liberty for a term of maximum two years, or short-term imprisonment for a term of maximum two months, or imprisonment for a term of maximum two years.

